# shell — caps.decl
#
# Wave: R49 (Wave 1)
# Doc:  design/tooling/r49-r50-plan.md §5.2 in the paideia-os repo.
#
# The shell is the process that reads user commands, spawns tool
# processes with the caller's cap environment narrowed per each
# callee's caps.decl, and threads text-and-schema layers through
# pipes. Its cap footprint at M1 is the minimum a running interactive
# prompt needs, mirroring the substrate the design doc names in §5.2:
#
#   * KIND_USER (0x190, paideia-os src/kernel/core/cap/kind_user.pdx)
#     — the shell runs as a delegated user; every child inherits the
#     caller's user identity by default (I6 capability handoff).
#   * KIND_TTY — the terminal-render binding; the shell holds
#     KIND_TTY(write) and delegates a sub-cap to each child. The
#     ordinal is TBD — kind_tty.pdx has not landed at HEAD (2026-08-21
#     kernel), so the shell M1 caps.decl names KIND_TTY symbolically;
#     libpdx-cap's caps_decl parser is textual and accepts the name
#     verbatim. shell.M2-001 pins the ordinal when the KIND lands.
#   * KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT (5, paideia-os src/kernel/core/cap/kind.pdx:72)
#     — the pipe substrate the shell mints one of per '|' at M2-002.
#     M1 declares the requirement so the exec-time manifest_verify
#     call at M2 does not need a signature change.
#   * KIND_SHELL_SESSION (0x194, allocated by this repo at M2-001,
#     derived over KIND_USER) — the shell mints this at session start
#     and hands sub-caps to `mux` splits and nested `remote`-shell
#     processes at R56+. M1 pre-declares the requirement so downstream
#     tooling (audit journal at M3, session lookup at M5) can already
#     see it in the manifest.
#   * KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write) (0x195, paideia-os
#     src/kernel/core/cap/kind_pdxfs_file.pdx, R42 scaffold) — the
#     shell writes CoW-journal records to `~/.history/` at every
#     interactive line commit. Encoder half landed at shell.M2-005;
#     runtime writer path landed at ENH-008 (#35): the shell now opens
#     `~/.history/<session>-<ts>.pdxhist` via
#     `sys_open(O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_APPEND)` at startup and drains the
#     encoded HistoryEntry ring to disk via `sys_write` after every
#     REPL step. Write cap is narrowed per-session to the invoker's
#     own history subtree via libpdx-cap's cap_pack_narrowed at
#     session start; children never receive this cap (the history
#     subtree is the shell's own state, not a child's). Verified
#     against src/session.pdx::session_derive_subcap (M2-001), which
#     only mints KIND_SHELL_SESSION sub-caps with SS_RIGHTS_CHILD
#     (0x3 = read | write, no mint) and never touches KIND_PDXFS_FILE
#     of any shape -- the history-write authority is per-shell state,
#     not per-session state, so the derivation surface does not
#     propagate it. Runtime persistence proof (reboot-across boundary)
#     is a paideia-os boot smoke, not a shell repo test.
#
# InitCap sidecar note. The R20b.M4-001 loader-side InitCap sidecar
# (paideia-os src/kernel/core/loader/init_caps.pdx) is not itself a
# KIND — it is the wire format the loader uses to seed a process's
# cap_table at exec. The shell relies on the sidecar (a child receives
# its argv-parallel caps that way at M2-002) but does not need to
# declare it here; the sidecar is a producer of caps, and the caps
# themselves are what caps.decl names.
requires:
- KIND_USER(read)
- KIND_TTY(write)
- KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT(mint)
- KIND_SHELL_SESSION(mint)
- KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write)

# Declared output schemas — the shell emits three schemas over the
# semantic-pipe substrate.
#
# - ShellPromptRecord — one record per interactive prompt (M3-001)
# - CommandCompletion — one array per tab-completion request (M3-002)
# - ShellCommandRecord — one record per command exec + wait (M3-003)
#
# At M3 the shell adds a fourth output PATH: it forwards its
# children's schema pipes UNCHANGED to the pipeline consumer (D2
# literal, pipe_passthrough.pdx). The forwarded schema is whatever
# the child declared; the shell is a transparent conduit, not a
# schema publisher for those bytes. Hence only the three names
# above appear here.
declares_output_schemas:
- ShellPromptRecord
- CommandCompletion
- ShellCommandRecord
